BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-200335@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20260917T170000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260917T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260917T183000
SUMMARY:Author Talk: "Driven" With Architect Patrick Ahearn 
LOCATION:Reading Room
DESCRIPTION:Category: The Arts\nPrice: Free\nAvailability: 27 spots left\nS
 tatus: Available\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/20033
 5\n\n5:00PM Reception\, 5:30PM Discussion\nJoin award-winning classical ar
 chitect and impassioned car collector Patrick Ahearn for an exclusive pre-
 launch discussion of his forthcoming book\, Driven: The Road to Iconic Des
 ign. At the intersection of his two greatest passions\, architecture and a
 utomobiles\, Driven explores Ahearn’s lifelong pursuit of the extraordin
 ary through bespoke carriage houses that distinguish many of his legacy pr
 operties and classic cars that have influenced his design purview.\n\nThro
 ugh more than a dozen signature projects\, Ahearn reveals carriage houses 
 that function as elegant entertaining spaces\, guest retreats\, anglers’
  lounges\, collector’s galleries\, and more. Cars of significance are wo
 ven within the narrative and photographed against the backdrop of Ahearn�
 �s homes\, creating a compelling dialogue between forms of excellence.\n\n
 Featuring captivating photography and personal narrative\, Driven is both 
 a celebration of historically inspired architecture and a reflection on Ah
 earn’s remarkable design journey. Members will hear firsthand about the 
 experiences\, influences\, automobiles\, and philosophy that have shaped h
 is career and fueled his enduring pursuit of iconic design\n\n*This event 
 is complimentary and reserved for members only. Complimentary light bites 
 and refreshments will be served. We kindly ask that all cancellations be m
 ade at least 24 hours prior to the start of the event.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/200335
CATEGORIES:The Arts
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-201263@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20260917T173000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260917T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260917T203000
SUMMARY: Wines of South America with Amanda Barnes
LOCATION:Lunasol
DESCRIPTION:Category: Food & Beverage\nPrice: $95.00 per person\nStatus: Wa
 itlist Only\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/201263\n\n
 5:30PM Reception\, 6:00PM Dinner\n\nIn celebration of Hispanic Heritage M
 onth\, enjoy an immersive dinner exploring flavor\, culture\, and story a
 longside Master of Wine\, Amanda Barnes. Author of the acclaimed The South
  America Wine Guide and a leading voice on the region’s wines\, Barnes w
 ill guide members through a thoughtfully curated tasting of exceptional se
 lections from across South America\, each chosen to showcase the diversity
  and character of this dynamic wine landscape.\n\nJourney from Garzón Pin
 ot Noir Rosé and vibrant whites from Chile\, Uruguay\, and Argentina to 
 expressive lighter reds\, before culminating with three iconic pours: Nico
 lás Catena Zapata\, Cheval des Andes\, and VIK. Paired with a thoughtful
 ly crafted plated dinner\, each wine will reveal the distinctive grapes\, 
 regions\, and traditions shaping South American wine today.\n\n*This event
  is offered at $95 per person\, plus tax\, and is reserved for members on
 ly. Tickets are nonrefundable.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/201263
CATEGORIES:Food & Beverage
END:VEVENT
